{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/648663-new-york-for-demon","id":648663,"title":"New York for Demon","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-02T01:54:23-07:00","id":648663,"title":"New York for Demon","content":"Looking for interesting places to put Infrastructure in, and I'm interested in more.. strange places then what a simple &quot;points of interest&quot; google search shows me. Anyone got ideas? Place and what kind of infrastructure might be there would be awesome.<br /> <br /> Currently, I have Rikers Island (the abusive prison institution), Manhattan Psychiatric Center, some U.S. Army Recruitment stuff (but that's mostly because one of the players decided for his Cover to be a military recruiter).<br /> <br /> EDIT: Found this gold mine <a href=\"http://www.newyork.com/articles/neighborhoods/the-10-weirdest-buildings-in-new-york-city-80414/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.newyork.com/articles/neig...rk-city-80414/</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":294,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","user":"Griautis","date":". 09-02-2015, 06:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T04:44:17-07:00","id":648743,"title":"","content":"I'm in a Demon game that takes place in Long Island with trips to NYC, and the first &quot;season&quot; of story arcs centered around connecting the Montauk Monster to Plum Island Animal Disease Center, a federal research facility with a history of biological weapon programs during the Cold War.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T08:51:07-07:00","id":651275,"title":"","content":"I'm running a game in NYC also helps being from NYC. NYC is broken up into Five Boroughs each one is so large that it could be its own state. So I like to think about NYC as the opposite of Seattle were its easy for demons the fall in Seattle its harder in NYC because this city is grids upon grids. Manhattan I believe the god machine would have insane amounts of control in Manhattan but not as much in the surrounding boroughs. <br /> <br /> So one of the more interesting things in NYC. <br /> <br /> Places like<br /> The Hidden Train station beneath City Hall<br /> <br /> Unknown Train Line (I don't remember what people are calling it.) People have seen it and some people were even on a train that got switched on to that line and it gets stranger. The train stopped at a station that had no markings and very few lights but that's not the strange part. The strange part is the fact that a bunch of beautiful party girls got off at that station. <br /> <br /> United Nations: I feel like would be some kind of command and control infrastructure <br /> <br /> The whole still working and intact Pneumatic Tube System. <br /> <br /> The Whole of the MTA subway train system has be some kind of infrastructure that I'm sure feeds on the anger on the lines because of how late they always are and also the fact so many insane people get on these things and randomly attack people. <br /> <br /> There are many gangs that spray paint occult stuff around the city what if it was for a reason ?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T07:56:28-07:00","id":656519,"title":"","content":"Any number oflarge chapels, churches or other places of worship<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.nycsubway.org/wiki/Abandoned_and_Disused_Stations\" target=\"_blank\">Abandoned Subway stations</a><br /> <br /> Museum of Modern Art (great place for dead drops, or taking kids, if any of your players have Offspring)<br /> <br /> 520 Madison Ave has five pieces of the Berlin Wall, if you want to do a Dark Eras tie-in.<br /> <br /> the Staten Island Boat Grave Yard<br /> <br /> Rockefeller Center<br /> <br /> JP Morgan Building","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}